---
title: Apple pie
servings: 8
yield: one 9-inch pie
tags: [american, vegetarian, thanksgiving, make-ahead]
cuisine: american
time: 2 hours
source: Apple Pie by Susan Reid, King Arthur Baking, https://www.kingarthurbaking.com/recipes/apple-pie-recipe
---

> Use the crust from Buttery pie crust (baking/pies-and-tarts), doubled, so
> there is one disc for the bottom and one for the top.

Heat the oven to 425°F (220°C). Lightly grease a #9-inch pie pan{}, ideally
1 1/2 to 2 inches deep.

== Filling ==

Toss the @apples{3.25%lb}(peeled and sliced 1/8 inch thick, about 8 cups) with
the @lemon juice{2%tbsp} in a #large bowl{}.

In a #small bowl{}, whisk the @granulated sugar{3/4%cup},
@all-purpose flour{2%tbsp}, @cornstarch{2%tbsp}, @table salt{1/2%tsp},
@ground cinnamon{1%tsp}, @ground nutmeg{1/4%tsp} and @ground allspice{1/4%tsp}.
Sprinkle over the apples and stir to coat. Stir in the
@boiled cider{1/4%cup}(or apple juice concentrate, optional) and
@vanilla extract{2%tsp}(optional).

== Assembly ==

Roll one disc of crust to a 12-inch round, lay it in the pan and trim to an inch
of overhang.

Spoon in the filling and dot with the @unsalted butter{2%tbsp}(diced).

Roll the second disc to a 12-inch round and lay it over the apples. Fold the
bottom overhang up over the top edge, pinch to seal and crimp. Prick the top all
over with a fork, or cut vents.

Chill the pie ~{10%minutes} while the oven finishes heating.

Set it on a parchment-lined #baking sheet{}. Brush the top with @whole milk{}
and sprinkle with @coarse sparkling sugar{}.

Bake ~{20%minutes}, then turn the oven to 375°F (190°C) and bake ~{40%minutes}
more, until the filling bubbles hard. Check at half an hour and shield the edges
with foil if they are browning fast.

Cool completely before slicing.

> The filling sets as it cools; cut it warm and it runs. Bake ahead and warm
> slices to serve.
